Originally, Muffet had an Epic Rarity, making her the 2nd card to get a change in Rarity (the 1st being the [http://undercards.wikia.com/wiki/Gaster_Blaster Gaster Blaster]). She had the stats of 6/6 with the cost of 8G. Her ability would make the owner heal 5 HP every time Muffet killed a monster whilst attacking. '''Alpha 2.7''' changed this to 4/9, possibly in an attempt to make her last and therefore heal longer as a buff.
With the release of [[Spider]] in Beta 5.2, '''Beta 5.3 '''buffed Muffet to summon a Spider as well as restoring 5 HP whenever she attacks and kills a monster. '''Beta 7.4''' buffed her a bit more by lowering her cost by 2G, but also decreasing her HP by 2.

And finally, '''Beta 8.1''' changed her completely by turning her into a legendary. As a 4/11 for 9G monster (thus getting +4 HP and +3 cost), she now puts 3 Spiders in both your and the opponent's deck, and will gain +2/+1 whenever one in summoned. '''Beta 9.3''' buffed her by also gaining Haste, much like Spider getting Haste in Beta 9.1. '''Beta 10.2''' buffed her again by making her also gain +2/+1 for every [http://undercards.wikia.com/wiki/Muffet's_Pet Muffet's Pet] summoned, but '''Beta 16.0''' nerfed her a bit by lowering her HP to 10. '''Beta 18.1''' nerfed her further by increasing her cost to 10G. This was returned to 9G in '''Beta 29.0'''.

'''Beta 46.0''' introduced the [https://undercards.fandom.com/wiki/Category:Arachnid Arachnid] Tribe and half a dozen new members of it. As a result, her effect was expended from just Spider and Muffet's Pet to all Arachnids. She was also made one herself, so the amount of different cards that affect her increased from 2 to 9. However, the effect no longer triggers from enemy monsters nor does it trigger from just summoning them. You need to play them (and a second Muffet is needed to buff the first).
